# The refusals of the lowering of md_alg.traverse_pairs
# (D[md-alg-traverse]), each a realistic bug of a pipeline or of a
# hand-written op. The program is that of
# ../MDExecToMDAlg/convert.mlir: a dual list of groups and two loops over it.
#
# RUN: mdir-opt %S/../MDExecToMDAlg/convert.mlir --md-exec-expose-validity \
# RUN:     --md-exec-choose-neighbors --md-exec-assign-algebra \
# RUN:     --md-exec-assign-storage=memory=device > %t.exec.mlir
# RUN: mdir-opt %t.exec.mlir --convert-md-exec-to-md-alg > %t.alg.mlir
#
# A pipeline that leaves out the converter: the big pass no longer lowers a
# loop over groups.
# RUN: not mdir-opt %t.exec.mlir --convert-md-exec-to-gpu 2>&1 \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=UNCONVERTED
# UNCONVERTED: 'md_exec.pair_for' op takes each pair once over groups, which 'convert-md-exec-to-md-alg' turns into 'md_alg.traverse_pairs' before this pass
#
# The buffer form in the pipeline: its contract is a precondition that its
# writer asserts, which the pipeline takes from the type instead.
# RUN: not mdir-opt %S/Inputs/traverse-buffers.mlir --convert-md-exec-to-gpu 2>&1 \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BUFFERS
# BUFFERS: 'md_alg.traverse_pairs' op takes its list as buffers, a form for the serial oracle and the tests; the pipeline takes the structure form, whose contract is in the type
#
# A cutoff beyond the reach that the structure was built for (D357).
# RUN: sed 's/cutoff(2.500000e+00) weights/cutoff(3.000000e+00) weights/' %t.alg.mlir \
# RUN: | not mdir-opt --convert-md-exec-to-gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=COVERAGE
# COVERAGE: 'md_alg.traverse_pairs' op the cutoff, 3.000000e+00, exceeds the cutoff that the neighbor structure was built with, 2.500000e+00
#
# The outer list of a dual list, which the loops take through the inner one.
# RUN: sed 's/ inner positions/ positions/' %t.alg.mlir \
# RUN: | not mdir-opt --convert-md-exec-to-gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OUTER
# OUTER: 'md_alg.traverse_pairs' op reads the outer list of a dual list, which the loops take through the inner list
#
# A stable visit, which the schedule of the groups does not give.
# RUN: sed 's/visit unordered/visit stable/' %t.alg.mlir \
# RUN: | not mdir-opt --convert-md-exec-to-gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=STABLE
# STABLE: 'md_alg.traverse_pairs' op visits its entries stably, which the schedule of the groups does not: its rotation and its atomics fix no tree
#
# A block that is not whole warps.
# RUN: not mdir-opt %t.alg.mlir --convert-md-exec-to-gpu=block-size=48 2>&1 \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BLOCK
# BLOCK: runs a warp for each unit of work, which needs blocks of whole warps, not 48 threads
#
# The serial oracle where the loop prunes for its refresh (D284).
# RUN: not mdir-opt %t.alg.mlir \
# RUN:     --convert-md-exec-to-gpu="fuse-pruning=true fuse-pruning-groups=7 traverse-oracle=serial" 2>&1 \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ORACLE
# ORACLE: 'md_alg.traverse_pairs' op prunes for its refresh (D284), which its serial definition does not: the oracle takes the pruning in the refresh
#
# An oracle that does not exist.
# RUN: not mdir-opt %t.alg.mlir --convert-md-exec-to-gpu=traverse-oracle=fast 2>&1 \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NAME
# NAME: has no lowering 'fast'
#
# The SIMT pattern on its own, and the serial definition of the structure
# form, which has no buffers on the host.
# RUN: not mdir-opt %t.alg.mlir --convert-md-alg-to-gpu 2>&1 \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ALONE
# ALONE: 'md_alg.traverse_pairs' op is lowered for a device by 'convert-md-exec-to-gpu', where it stands
# RUN: not mdir-opt %t.alg.mlir --convert-md-alg-to-scf 2>&1 \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SERIAL
# SERIAL: 'md_alg.traverse_pairs' op takes its list as a structure, which has no buffers on the host
